# Living Survey: rag_architecture                                                                                    
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Introduction                                                                                                      
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
This document collects the scientific literature regarding **rag_architecture**.                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Knowledge Graph Integration in RAG                                                                                
                                                                                                                     
Recent advancements have focused on hybridizing Retrieval-Augmented Generation with Knowledge Graphs (KGs) to        
mitigate hallucinations and improve structural coherence in complex reasoning tasks. GraphRAG frameworks leverage the
intrinsic relational nature of graphs to encode heterogeneous information, making it a golden resource for RAG       
applications [^10.48550_arxiv.2501.00309]. Furthermore, layered RAG pipelines that synthesize textual entity         
extraction, community summaries, and structural link navigation have been proposed to capture comprehensive contexts 
and mitigate hallucinations in knowledge-intensive domains [^10.36838_v6i12.11]. These approaches also extend to     
experimental software architectures that prioritize flexibility and traceability, integrating LLMs with RAG and KGs  
to improve management and verification of AI workflows [^10.1016_j.websem.2024.100853]. Furthermore, specialized     
biomedical applications have successfully leveraged Knowledge Graph RAG to enrich sequence embeddings with external  
biological context, significantly enhancing predictive performance for epitope discovery [^10.1021_acs.jcim.5c02248].
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Optimization and Filtering Mechanisms                                                                             
                                                                                                                     
To address the degradation of performance caused by irrelevant or noisy retrieved documents, novel filtering and     
scoring mechanisms have been introduced. MAIN-RAG employs a training-free, multi-agent framework that collaboratively
filters and scores retrieved documents using an adaptive relevance threshold, effectively minimizing noise while     
maintaining high recall and improving answer accuracy across QA benchmarks [^10.48550_arxiv.2501.00332].             
Additionally, optimizing the retrieval pipeline through dynamic chunking strategies and advanced vector search       
indices, such as FAISS HNSW combined with cross-encoder re-ranking, has proven effective in preserving contextual    
coherence and enhancing response fidelity without sacrificing computational efficiency [^10.56038_oprd.v5i1.516].    
Research into low-resource and morphologically complex languages demonstrates that RAG frameworks markedly improve   
information precision and contextual relevance, with models like LLaMA3.1-8B achieving equitable performance in      
Turkish question-answering tasks [^10.22531_muglajsci.1781095]. Additionally, integrating sentiment classification   
with retrieval-based techniques using FAISS indexing enhances contextual understanding and interpretability in       
customer feedback analysis [^10.22214_ijraset.2025.76657]. Recent advancements in multi-hop retrieval have           
highlighted that failures are not uniformly distributed but cluster in structurally predictable subpopulations. To   
address this, RegimeAbstain computes a Retrieval Confidence Score (RCS) based on query-ANN structural features,      
implementing a calibrated abstention policy that significantly reduces confident-wrong-answer rates without requiring
additional LLM calls [^2609.22056]. Similarly, managing conflicting retrieved memories remains a critical challenge; 
the Memory Decision Layer (MDL) introduces a zero-parameter controller that fuses relevance, reliability, and task   
risk through orthogonal subspace projection, explicitly decoupling confidence from consistency to reduce             
hallucination rates under conflicting memories by over 56% [^2609.22043]. Furthermore, bridging the semantic gap     
between retrievers and LLMs is crucial for relationship modeling. ConRAG employs a lightweight Con-Former model      
placed between the retriever and LLM to capture and transmit semantic information, enabling effective feature        
modeling and alignment even in low-resource scenarios where both components are frozen [^10.1145_3847108]. Finally,  
hierarchical retrieval strategies have proven effective for grounding synthetic outputs. AURORA-RAG integrates       
documentary evidence across country, community, and persona stages using Reciprocal Rank Fusion and Pseudo-Relevance 
Feedback, increasing corpus-supported claims to 91% and reducing hallucination frequency to 7%                       
[^10.20944_preprints202609.1600.v1].                                                                                 
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Instruction Tuning for RAG                                                                                        
                                                                                                                     
Expanding the applicability of RAG beyond limited scenarios requires diverse and high-quality instruction data.      
RAG-Instruct addresses this by synthesizing a comprehensive instruction dataset based on five distinct RAG paradigms 
and instruction simulation techniques, significantly boosting LLMs' zero-shot RAG capabilities across a wide range of
tasks [^10.48550_arxiv.2501.00353]. This methodology demonstrates that structured instruction tuning can effectively 
enhance zero-shot RAG performance across diverse tasks. Domain-specific prompt engineering and automated optimization
further enhance RAG reliability. An agency-specific project authoring advisor demonstrates that coupling LLMs with   
curated technical document databases via an end-to-end RAG pipeline, combined with automated adversarial prompt      
optimization, significantly improves answer comprehensiveness and accuracy [^10.1061_jccee5.cpeng-7192].             
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Human-Centered and Applied RAG                                                                                    
                                                                                                                     
The practical deployment of RAG architectures is increasingly being evaluated through human-centered and             
domain-specific lenses. In scientific literature classification, RAG-enhanced LLMs have demonstrated superior        
accuracy over traditional supervised models, even with limited labeled data, highlighting their adaptability to      
specialized linguistic corpora [^10.56977_jicce.2024.22.4.280]. Moreover, in humanitarian contexts, optimizing RAG   
hyperparameters through multi-criteria decision-making has shown promise in reducing carbon emissions and bias while 
ensuring fair, equitable, and non-discriminatory responses for vulnerable populations [^10.3390_app15010325]. In the 
domain of digital archives, integrated AI systems utilizing RAG have demonstrated superior retrieval accuracy and    
question-answering quality by unifying metadata modeling with semantic vector frameworks [^10.70695_iaai202504a7].   
Domain-specific implementations, such as BioChat for biodiversity conservation, utilize Re-Ranker-based routing      
within RAG pipelines to significantly boost factual accuracy and mitigate hallucinations compared to naive baselines 
[^10.3390_su18010396]. Systematic reviews of intelligent educational agents highlight that combining RAG with        
multi-source embeddings and adaptive difficulty tracking substantially improves contextual accuracy and learner      
engagement [^10.55041_ijsrem55690]. Pedagogical designs for multi-persona AI tutors also employ retrieval-augmented  
generation alongside provenance cues to reduce hallucination risks while prioritizing process quality over direct    
answer generation [^10.3390_asi9010017]. In high-performance computing environments, AskALCF addresses complex user  
support challenges by indexing public documentation into a vector store and exposing live cluster state via Model    
Context Protocol (MCP) servers, enabling agents to combine documentation with operational context in a single tool   
call [^10.5281_zenodo.22804496]. In scientific collaborations, Data Sherpa provides context-aware access to scattered
knowledge by migrating onto Open WebUI for local model deployment and multi-agent workflows, emphasizing data        
sovereignty and the ability to explicitly acknowledge uncertainty [^10.5281_zenodo.22804319]. Additionally,          
journalistic workflows have explored cooperative production models where modular storytelling and RAG architectures  
preserve editorial control while enabling AI-assisted contextual generation and personalized news consumption        
[^10.5281_zenodo.20258770].                                                                                          
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Semantic Governance and Ethical Implications                                                                      
                                                                                                                     
Emerging research critically examines the architectural limitations of source-grounding in RAG systems. Empirical    
tests across multiple RAG implementations reveal that mere source access does not prevent semantic governance        
failures or hallucinations under strict semantic dominance, indicating a need for advanced governance primitives     
[^10.5281_zenodo.18039273]. Furthermore, privacy benchmarks indicate that standard RAG assistants can inadvertently  
leak sensitive user data in over 26% of interactions, underscoring the necessity for privacy-by-design structural    
safeguards in personalized AI deployments [^10.48550_arxiv.2512.24848]. Privacy and capability separation are also   
critical in specialized hiring platforms. The NeuroMatch Agentic RAG architecture introduces Identity and Capability 
Separation (ICS) to decouple personally identifiable information from capability data before semantic indexing,      
combining deterministic constraints with human approval gates to ensure fairness and privacy in decision-support     
systems [^10.6084_m9.figshare.33941032].                                                                             
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Advanced RAG Architectures                                                                                        
                                                                                                                     
Beyond standard QA, RAG principles are being adapted for complex agentic workflows. The R-Debater framework          
introduces argumentative memory and retrieval grounding to generate coherent, stance-aligned multi-turn debates,     
demonstrating that combining retrieval with structured planning yields more faithful and logically consistent outputs
[^https:__openalex.org_W7118051612]. Structured multimodal frameworks are also emerging to enforce strict knowledge  
boundaries. WILDFLOW introduces an architectural control layer that prioritizes structured Markdown files as the     
authoritative source of truth, enforces unit-level vector database isolation, and restricts LLM usage to             
classification and verification, transforming retrieval into a verification-driven pipeline optimized for educational
environments [^10.5281_zenodo.18911616].                                                                             
                                                                                                                     

