 ## Introduction                                                                                                     
 ## Knowledge Graph Integration in RAG                                                                               
 Recent advancements have focused on hybridizing Retrieval-Augmented Generation with Knowledge Graphs (KGs) to       
mitigate hallucinations and improve structural coherence in complex reasoning tasks. GraphRAG frameworks leverage the
intrinsic relational nature of graphs to encode heterogeneous information, making it a golden resource for RAG       
applications [^10.48550_arxiv.2501.00309]. Furthermore, layered RAG pipelines that synthesize textual entity         
extraction, community summaries, and structural link navigation have been proposed to capture comprehensive contexts 
and mitigate hallucinations in knowledge-intensive domains [^10.36838_v6i12.11]. These approaches also extend to     
experimental software architectures that prioritize flexibility and traceability, integrating LLMs with RAG and KGs  
to improve management and verification of AI workflows [^10.1016_j.websem.2024.100853]. Furthermore, specialized     
                                                                                                                     
 ## Human-Centered and Applied RAG                                                                                   
-The practical deployment of RAG architectures is increasingly being evaluated through human-centered and            
domain-specific lenses. In scientific literature classification, RAG-enhanced LLMs have demonstrated superior        
accuracy over traditional supervised models, even with limited labeled data, highlighting their adaptability to      
specialized linguistic corpora [^10.56977_jicce.2024.22.4.280]. Moreover, in humanitarian contexts, optimizing RAG   
hyperparameters through multi-criteria decision-making has shown promise in reducing carbon emissions and bias while 
ensuring fair, equitable, and non-discriminatory responses for vulnerable populations [^10.3390_app15010325]. In the 
domain of digital archives, integrated AI systems utilizing RAG have demonstrated superior retrieval accuracy and    
question-answering quality by unifying metadata modeling with semantic vector frameworks [^10.70695_iaai202504a7].   
Domain-specific implementations, such as BioChat for biodiversity conservation, utilize Re-Ranker-based routing      
within RAG pipelines to significantly boost factual accuracy and mitigate hallucinations compared to naive baselines 
[^10.3390_su18010396]. Systematic reviews of intelligent educational agents highlight that combining RAG with        
multi-source embeddings and adaptive difficulty tracking substantially improves contextual accuracy and learner      
engagement [^10.55041_ijsrem55690]. Pedagogical designs for multi-persona AI tutors also employ retrieval-augmented  
generation alongside provenance cues to reduce hallucination risks while prioritizing process quality over direct    
answer generation [^10.3390_asi9010017]. In high-performance computing environments, AskALCF addresses complex user  
support challenges by indexing public documentation into a vector store and exposing live cluster state via Model    
Context Protocol (MCP) servers, enabling agents to combine documentation with operational context in a single tool   
call [^10.5281_zenodo.22804496]. In scientific collaborations, Data Sherpa provides context-aware access to scattered
knowledge by migrating onto Open WebUI for local model deployment and multi-agent workflows, emphasizing data        
sovereignty and the ability to explicitly acknowledge uncertainty [^10.5281_zenodo.22804319]. Additionally,          
journalistic workflows have explored cooperative production models where modular storytelling and RAG architectures  
preserve editorial control while enabling AI-assisted contextual generation and personalized news consumption        
[^10.5281_zenodo.20258770].                                                                                          
